Skip AVI chunks whose size does not fit the int packet size.

avi_sync() (libavformat/avidec.c) bounds a chunk size only by the file size, and that is the
RIFF size when the I/O size is smaller, so sizes up to 4 GiB pass. packet_size = size + 8 and
remaining = size are ints: for size > INT_MAX - 8 packet_size goes negative (signed overflow)
and ni_prepare_read() later fails av_assert0(best_ast->remaining <= best_ast->packet_size)
(avidec.c:1465) once the demuxer has switched to non-interleaved reading. Whether it gets
there depends on how the int overflow in pos += packet_size - remaining is compiled: wasm32
builds reach the assertion, an x86_64 clang -O1 build fails the seek first. Treat such a
chunk header as no sync point.
Not fixed upstream as of 50276fac71 (2026-11-23).

Includes libavformat/tests/avi_chunk_size.c (fate-avi-chunk-size): a hand-made AVI with a
4 GiB RIFF size and a second movi chunk of 0x7ffffffc bytes. Without the fix that chunk comes
out as a truncated packet; the test expects only the first one.

Upstream: none found.

